From a4c089c7b1dff7f1c794d93bdcf15e7fb061770a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:04:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(emitter): hoist undecorated classes' named-evaluation
 keys into the enclosing environment

The undecorated branch of visitClassDeclaration/visitClassExpression
(_tsc.js 99628, `enterClass(undefined)`) still visits every member through
classElementVisitor, so visitPropertyDeclaration performs the named evaluation
of an anonymous decorated class initializer: getAssignedNameOfPropertyName
hoists `getGeneratedNameForNode(name)` into the innermost lexical environment
(the enclosing function body via visitFunctionBody, or the source file via
visitEachChild(SourceFile) -> visitLexicalEnvironment) and rewrites the name to
`[_a = __propKey(expression)]`; the class receives `__setFunctionName(this,
_a)`, and class-fields lowering later reads the cache assignment as already
transformed. The Rust member loop of undecorated classes recorded literal names
only, and the source-file visit owned no lexical environment.

`visit_class_members_generic` now runs `prepare_property_named_evaluation`
inside the class-element frame (hoist, rewrite, previsit under the name frame),
and `transform_root` starts the source-file environment around the visit and
merges its hoisted `var` statement after the prologue directives and any
custom-prologue hoisted functions (`merge_source_file_environment`,
mergeLexicalEnvironment's `leftHoistedFunctionsEnd`). Function bodies keep
`visit_function_like_body`'s environment.

Focused witnesses: undecorated-outer-property-hoist x6 and
decorated-outer-property-hoist-control x6 exact twice, exit 0
(ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-followup-cause3-focused.v1.json); the 18 top-level
commands (plain, `"use strict"` prologue, decorated control) exact twice, exit 0
(ratchets/h2-8a-decorator-followup-top-level-focused.v1.json).
